    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as our definitive anchor, boasting an elite 83.29 score. Facing Matthews, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a favorable matchup against a starter with a 4.32 xERA and a generous 100% stolen base success rate against the opposing delivery, maximizing his potential to contribute in our scarcest category. Meanwhile, **Drake Baldwin** (68.18) stands out as our premier secondary play; despite a tricky left-handed matchup against Thornton, his recent form and a solid 0.377 xwOBA profile position him for a strong offensive output out of the two-hole. **Kyle Tucker** (63.95) and **Sam Antonacci** (63.14) also offer high-floor utility, with **Sam Antonacci** specifically benefiting from a significant 19% SP skill boost against Lowder, whose 4.76 xERA represents one of the softer targets on the board today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s card involved **Wade Meckler** (59.97) and **Andy Pages** (59.34), who both hovered right on the edge of our efficiency threshold. **Wade Meckler** ultimately held his spot in the OF5 slot due to his premier leadoff position and a distinct platoon advantage against Quantrill, whereas **Andy Pages** remains a high-value utility option despite the tough assignment against Lynch IV. **Heliot Ramos** (46.67) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (51.27) present the highest degree of risk; both are fighting sub-optimal platoon splits against Miller and Mahle, respectively, and we are monitoring them closely to ensure they don't drag down our daily efficiency. We continue to manage the absence of **Jordan Westburg** and **Josh Jung**, leaving **Coby Mayo** as the primary depth option, though he remains on the bench today as he is currently absent from the confirmed starting lineup.",
